1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
‪FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:43,543
<i>‪I found out who ordered</i>
<i>‪Choi Jeong-yo's abduction.</i>

3
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,291
<i>‪Hello, Mr. Kang.</i>

4
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,002
‪Where did you get this photo?

5
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:28,338
‪Are you positive?
‪Is this information accurate?

6
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:30,215
<i>‪Yes, I'm positive.</i>

7
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:32,634
<i>‪I got my hands on the secret footage</i>

8
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:34,761
<i>‪that the local middlemen had taken</i>
<i>‪just in case.</i>

9
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,262
<i>‪And I got their firsthand accounts.</i>

10
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:38,473
‪That can't be right.
‪There's been a mistake.

11
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,100
‪The news clearly stated

12
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:43,353
‪that terrorists were behind it.

13
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:45,522
‪They emailed the competition committee
‪demanding a ransom--

14
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:48,608
<i>‪That's a common tactic used</i>
<i>‪to </i><i>‪cause </i><i>‪confusion.</i>

15
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:52,153
<i>‪Are you all right?</i>

16
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:56,074
‪So what were their orders?

17
00:01:57,492 --> 00:01:58,409
‪Were they told

18
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:01,162
‪to kill him?

19
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:05,917
<i>‪No.</i>

20
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,961
<i>‪The order was to hold him</i>
<i>‪and release him later.</i>

21
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:10,296
<i>‪But things went sideways.</i>

22
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:12,507
<i>‪The person in the photo…</i>

23
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:15,426
<i>‪is your mother, right?</i>

24
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:36,364
‪FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

25
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:38,950
‪EPISODE 9

26
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:07,562
‪Wasn't Pi-o absolutely amazing today?

27
00:03:07,645 --> 00:03:09,063
‪Totally.

28
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:11,691
‪He absolutely killed it.

29
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:13,818
‪I knew he could do it.

30
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,653
‪That slump he was in?

31
00:03:15,737 --> 00:03:17,530
‪I knew he'd get over it before long.

32
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:19,908
‪Because Pi-o is

33
00:03:20,533 --> 00:03:23,912
‪a special gift sent to me from God.

34
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:25,455
‪Agreed.

35
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:27,749
‪To your son, Pi-o Kang.

36
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:32,170
‪He's totally a gift from the heavens.

37
00:03:36,507 --> 00:03:40,678
‪From the moment I discovered his talent,

38
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:45,391
‪I never once doubted
‪he'd become a great pianist.

39
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:47,185
‪I clearly saw it coming.

40
00:03:47,977 --> 00:03:49,812
‪So I did everything I could.

41
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:52,899
‪I did whatever it took for Pi-o.

42
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:56,694
‪That's what made Pi-o who he is today.

43
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,071
‪Don't you agree?

44
00:03:58,154 --> 00:03:59,239
‪I do.

45
00:03:59,739 --> 00:04:02,659
‪You're really amazing.

46
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,495
‪But please don't forget

47
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:09,624
‪that we set the stage for them
‪at the right moment.

48
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:12,252
‪Pairing two people
‪with that kind of chemistry

49
00:04:12,335 --> 00:04:14,879
‪is what created that magic, right?

50
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:17,924
‪You're right.

51
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:21,636
‪They certainly have a special chemistry.

52
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:41,197
‪Gosh, you scared me.

53
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:44,659
‪Pi-o.

54
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,828
‪Is the after-party already over?

55
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,206
‪Why are you here?

56
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,835
‪Did you stay up to see me?

57
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:58,589
‪I was so happy today.

58
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:03,594
‪I knew you would do a phenomenal job.

59
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:07,015
‪Tell everyone who said you hit a slump
‪to show their faces.

60
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,318
‪What's wrong?

61
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:21,696
‪Why did you do it, Mom?

62
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,489
‪What do you mean?

63
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:26,200
‪Why did you hire someone
‪to abduct Jeong-yo?

64
00:05:28,578 --> 00:05:30,371
‪I don't know what you're talking about.

65
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:37,295
‪How could someone do that
‪to another person?

66
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:40,173
‪How could you commit a crime like that?

67
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:41,924
‪I knew you doubted me,

68
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:44,302
‪but what on earth were you thinking?

69
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,973
‪I have no idea what you're saying.

70
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:50,725
‪Hire? Abduct?

71
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:54,270
‪How could you accuse me
‪of something so horrifying?

72
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:02,612
‪Where…

73
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:05,865
‪Where did you get this photo?

74
00:06:05,948 --> 00:06:07,033
‪That's not the point.

75
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:08,409
‪I asked you a question!

76
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:11,621
‪I got it from the middlemen
‪you hired for the abduction.

77
00:06:11,704 --> 00:06:12,580
‪So?

78
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:15,208
‪Will you still deny it?

79
00:06:29,097 --> 00:06:29,931
‪You're right.

80
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:32,433
‪I ordered the abduction.

81
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:37,897
‪It was the finals,
‪and you hurt your finger.

82
00:06:39,273 --> 00:06:40,358
‪I couldn't think straight.

83
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:44,112
‪I devoted my entire life
‪to seeing you win,

84
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:46,280
‪but you said you'd quit if you didn't.

85
00:06:46,364 --> 00:06:47,865
‪It drove me insane.

86
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:49,325
‪But Pi-o,

87
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:51,661
‪I need you to know this.

88
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:55,498
‪I had no intention of killing him.

89
00:06:55,581 --> 00:06:58,292
‪I told them to keep him for a bit
‪and let him go.

90
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:00,920
‪I thought about everything
‪from turning myself in

91
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:02,171
‪to coming clean to you.

92
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:03,089
‪But then…

93
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:08,136
‪Then you won first place
‪at the competition.

94
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:13,558
‪I couldn't lay that disgrace on you.

95
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:16,060
‪Not after everything
‪you went through to earn it.

96
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:18,938
‪You understand

97
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,399
‪why I had to do it, right?

98
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:25,403
‪I just wanted the best for you.

99
00:07:26,195 --> 00:07:27,113
‪It was for you.

100
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:29,407
‪Stop talking nonsense!

101
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:33,244
‪Did you think about
‪how disgraceful it'd be to win like that?

102
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:34,787
‪Because of that accident,

103
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:37,290
‪Jeong-yo can't play the piano anymore
‪and lost his memories!

104
00:07:37,373 --> 00:07:39,625
‪It was hard for me too!

105
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,962
‪I thought I had lost my mind
‪and regretted it so much.

106
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:46,174
‪I haven't slept peacefully
‪since that happened.

107
00:07:46,257 --> 00:07:47,133
‪But…

108
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:50,595
‪what can we do about it now?

109
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:52,805
‪If the truth comes out,

110
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:56,058
‪both of our lives will be over.

111
00:07:56,642 --> 00:07:58,144
‪How could I possibly live like that?

112
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:01,022
‪People will point fingers at me,
‪saying I ruined your life.

113
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,192
‪I wouldn't last a single day of that.

114
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,736
‪If you commit a crime,

115
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,196
‪you should be punished.

116
00:08:08,279 --> 00:08:09,697
‪That goes for both of us.

117
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:11,866
‪Let's go.

118
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:13,784
‪We'll confess to Jeong-yo
‪and ask for his forgiveness.

119
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:15,495
‪No, I won't go!

120
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:18,623
‪Jeong-yo didn't die after all,

121
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:20,666
‪and now…

122
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,085
‪now we're back to where we started.

123
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:30,718
‪Pi-o.

124
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:33,054
‪As long as we bury this secret,

125
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:36,057
‪we can go on living like nothing happened.

126
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,141
<i>‪So please…</i>

127
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:40,978
<i>‪Do you hear yourself?</i>

128
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,730
<i>‪That won't make the crime just disappear.</i>

129
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:44,732
‪Mom.

130
00:08:45,316 --> 00:08:48,027
‪Do you really want to hit rock bottom?

131
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,404
‪Come on.

132
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,490
‪Let's go and tell him everything.

133
00:08:52,573 --> 00:08:54,534
‪No!

134
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:58,871
‪I'd rather die

135
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,832
‪than let anyone know about this.

136
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:03,709
‪Are you…

137
00:09:04,502 --> 00:09:06,420
‪willing to let me die like this?

138
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:54,695
‪What brings you here at this hour?

139
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:05,164
‪What is this about? Why are you stalling?

140
00:11:05,247 --> 00:11:06,457
‪Go on, tell me.

141
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:13,589
‪You don't look well.

142
00:11:14,715 --> 00:11:16,133
‪Are you hiding something from me?

143
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:25,184
‪Yes.

144
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:28,854
‪So I'm here to ask for your forgiveness.

145
00:11:32,149 --> 00:11:34,693
‪Nine years ago
‪at the Harmonie International Competition…

146
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:39,365
<i>‪I'd rather die</i>

147
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,659
‪than let anyone know about this.

148
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:42,660
‪Are you…

149
00:11:43,536 --> 00:11:46,747
‪willing to let me die like this?

150
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:57,967
‪I was able to win the competition

151
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:01,053
‪because of your sheet music.

152
00:12:02,304 --> 00:12:04,807
‪I'd lost the sheet music for the set piece
‪at the chapel,

153
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,100
‪so I was going to withdraw.

154
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:09,228
‪But you lent me yours.

155
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:12,022
‪I only managed to play so well

156
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:14,608
‪thanks to the notes you left.

157
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,361
‪So where I stand right now…

158
00:12:20,531 --> 00:12:21,490
‪belongs to you.

159
00:12:23,075 --> 00:12:25,327
‪I didn't have the courage
‪to tell you the truth before.

160
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:31,333
‪I'm sorry.

161
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:50,478
‪That's it?

162
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:53,898
‪That's what you wanted to tell me?

163
00:12:55,191 --> 00:12:56,984
‪I don't quite understand.

164
00:12:57,067 --> 00:12:58,486
‪All this over sheet music?

165
00:12:59,487 --> 00:13:00,946
‪Interpreting it is one thing.

166
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,741
‪But how you play it is another matter.

167
00:13:05,701 --> 00:13:06,660
‪I watched

168
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:09,580
‪a video of your competition performance.

169
00:13:10,664 --> 00:13:13,292
‪You had a distinct style
‪that went beyond interpretation.

170
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:16,462
‪Anyway, I don't care about
‪things like that.

171
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,089
‪Come on.

172
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:24,220
‪You had me scared
‪because you looked so serious.

173
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:05,427
‪CHOI JEONG-YO

174
00:14:22,861 --> 00:14:26,365
‪MOM

175
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:32,204
<i>‪The call cannot be connected.</i>

176
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:35,332
<i>‪You will be connected to voicemail</i>
<i>‪after the beep,</i>

177
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:36,542
<i>‪and call charges will apply.</i>

178
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:54,727
‪Where were you?

179
00:14:59,773 --> 00:15:00,774
‪Pi-o.

180
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:03,444
‪Did you tell him?

181
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:05,613
‪You told him?

182
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:20,377
‪Go inside.

183
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:35,142
‪What is it?

184
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:38,854
‪I didn't get a chance
‪to tell you something.

185
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,190
‪Can I come in?

186
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,282
‪This is a nice practice room.

187
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:53,535
‪You get great sunlight.

188
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:57,623
‪The music would just play itself
‪in a room like this.

189
00:15:58,415 --> 00:15:59,667
‪What did you want to tell me?

190
00:16:00,417 --> 00:16:01,251
‪Right.

191
00:16:08,676 --> 00:16:09,551
‪What's this?

192
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:11,553
‪It's the piano concerto I composed.

193
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:14,098
‪It took me five years to finish.

194
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:17,101
‪I felt it was time
‪to share this with the world,

195
00:16:17,184 --> 00:16:19,603
‪so I've been looking for
‪a soloist to play it.

196
00:16:20,562 --> 00:16:21,480
‪Mr. Kang.

197
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,483
‪Please be the first to play this.

198
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,112
‪I can't.

199
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:29,947
‪Why not?

200
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,699
‪I already told you. I…

201
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:36,620
‪I have no right to play that.

202
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:38,789
‪And I already told you.

203
00:16:39,623 --> 00:16:42,918
‪I merely provided the interpretation.
‪You won first place on your own merits.

204
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:46,922
‪At least check it out
‪before you shut me down.

205
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,341
‪You haven't even looked at it.

206
00:17:44,813 --> 00:17:45,814
‪Just as I thought.

207
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:47,608
‪I can't do it.

208
00:17:47,691 --> 00:17:50,027
‪Why not? You don't like the piece?

209
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,738
‪No, the piece is beautiful.

210
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:56,366
‪I can tell how much effort
‪you put into it.

211
00:17:57,493 --> 00:17:59,661
‪Everyone will be stunned
‪when it comes out.

212
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:01,121
‪Then why won't you do it?

213
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:03,665
‪Just…

214
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:08,545
‪Just find someone else.

215
00:18:09,671 --> 00:18:11,381
‪I just told you.

216
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:17,721
‪I've looked everywhere,
‪and you're the one I want.

217
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:21,183
‪I don't need just any pianist.

218
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:25,145
‪I need someone as dedicated as I am
‪who will pour their soul into it.

219
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:28,524
‪Our recent performance
‪made me even more certain.

220
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:31,068
‪The only person
‪who would give it their all

221
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,278
‪is you, Mr. Kang.

222
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:37,407
‪What if we look at it this way?

223
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:42,079
‪If you've been
‪torturing yourself with guilt,

224
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,500
‪use this as an opportunity
‪to make it up to me.

225
00:18:47,751 --> 00:18:49,002
‪Still not interested?

226
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:54,216
‪If you won't do it,
‪I won't release the piece.

227
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:56,760
‪So choose your answer wisely.

228
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,222
‪I'm going to wait until you say yes.

229
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:09,481
‪I'll be off then.

230
00:19:11,233 --> 00:19:12,818
‪I'll be looking forward to good news.

231
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,213
‪What did he mean by that?

232
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:34,673
‪Do what together?

233
00:19:34,756 --> 00:19:36,049
‪Were you eavesdropping?

234
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,470
‪What did he mean by you feeling guilty?

235
00:19:40,554 --> 00:19:42,264
‪How much did you tell him?

236
00:19:42,806 --> 00:19:45,058
‪I didn't tell him about you, so just stop.

237
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:47,519
‪Stay out of my business.

238
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:54,109
<i>‪You asked me before</i>

239
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:57,070
‪why I'm conducting instead of playing.

240
00:19:57,654 --> 00:19:58,697
‪Nine years ago,

241
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,575
‪I got shot in my right shoulder.

242
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:04,203
<i>‪It caused nerve damage in my fingers.</i>

243
00:20:04,286 --> 00:20:06,955
<i>‪I can get through daily life,</i>
<i>‪but I can't play anymore.</i>

244
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:11,168
<i>‪Take away music from a musician,</i>
<i>‪and he's left with hell.</i>

245
00:20:12,544 --> 00:20:13,629
‪But a slump…

246
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:17,090
‪is something you can work your way out of.

247
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:19,384
<i>‪That's not the case for me.</i>

248
00:20:20,636 --> 00:20:22,512
<i>‪I'm actually envious of you.</i>

249
00:20:28,936 --> 00:20:30,896
<i>‪If you've been</i>
<i>‪torturing yourself with guilt,</i>

250
00:20:32,439 --> 00:20:35,275
<i>‪use this as an opportunity</i>
<i>‪to make it up to me.</i>

251
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:50,040
‪CHOI JEONG-YO:
‪HOW LONG WILL YOU KEEP ME WAITING?

252
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:52,042
‪IF YOU FEEL BAD ABOUT THE PAST,
‪THEN JUST DO IT.

253
00:21:27,995 --> 00:21:28,912
‪I'll do it.

254
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:32,207
‪If that's what you want,
‪I'll give it my best.

255
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:35,794
‪But if you're not satisfied…

256
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,339
‪you can replace me anytime.

257
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,258
‪I genuinely want to make an effort…

258
00:21:44,553 --> 00:21:45,846
‪for your sake.

259
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:52,978
‪You composed this?

260
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:54,563
‪Yes, sir.

261
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,734
‪It's not bad for your first piece.

262
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,279
‪The only thing is…

263
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:06,116
‪Were you thinking of someone
‪when you composed this?

264
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,201
‪How strange.

265
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:12,539
‪Why do I hear the composer's narrative
‪before the music itself?

266
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:16,877
‪I'm not sure.

267
00:22:18,211 --> 00:22:20,839
‪I just tried to put
‪my true feelings into it.

268
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:25,886
‪So,

269
00:22:25,969 --> 00:22:28,889
‪why did you show this to me?

270
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:32,809
‪I was hoping…

271
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:38,607
‪to premiere this piece at the orchestra's
‪80th anniversary festival.

272
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:42,027
‪What do you think of it, Mr. Kang?

273
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:43,904
‪All right.

274
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:46,448
‪Go ahead and do it.

275
00:22:49,034 --> 00:22:49,993
‪However,

276
00:22:50,744 --> 00:22:54,748
‪I hope the performance
‪can move beyond personal sentiment

277
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:58,502
‪and become a piece
‪that speaks to everyone.

278
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:00,587
‪Can you do that?

279
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:02,798
‪Yes, sir.

280
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:06,426
‪Is there a soloist you have in mind?

281
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:09,596
‪Yes, I do.

282
00:23:12,432 --> 00:23:13,767
‪Pianist Kang Pi-o.

283
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:19,106
‪Pi-o?

284
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:22,400
‪Really?

285
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:27,906
‪How about a more explosive
‪and powerful pianist?

286
00:23:28,698 --> 00:23:31,827
‪I believe he has that kind of potential.

287
00:23:33,036 --> 00:23:34,412
‪And I can draw it out of him.

288
00:23:44,297 --> 00:23:46,091
‪This is a beautiful piece.

289
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:56,309
‪Pi-o is truly so lucky.

290
00:24:13,743 --> 00:24:15,620
‪May I ask you something?

291
00:24:16,413 --> 00:24:17,497
‪Yes.

292
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:22,294
‪You seem unusually harsh on Pi-o.

293
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:27,174
‪He's had a lot of success
‪and earned a reputation.

294
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:29,384
‪Isn't it time to acknowledge him?

295
00:24:30,218 --> 00:24:31,553
‪So why do you still--

296
00:24:31,636 --> 00:24:33,430
‪He takes after me.

297
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,267
‪He'll push himself to the limit…

298
00:24:40,103 --> 00:24:42,856
‪then choose to self-destruct
‪if it doesn't work out.

299
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:45,442
‪You see,

300
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:50,238
‪art is a nasty beast that won't rest
‪until it drains you dry.

301
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:58,371
‪It does that even to talented musicians.

302
00:25:00,916 --> 00:25:01,917
‪Just imagine…

303
00:25:04,544 --> 00:25:06,546
‪what it would do to those who aren't.

304
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,811
‪Goodness, you're amazing.

305
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:24,856
‪Jeong-yo.

306
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:28,485
‪In addition to premiering this piece,

307
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:31,488
‪how about releasing an album
‪before the 80th anniversary festival?

308
00:25:31,571 --> 00:25:33,490
‪-An album?
‪-Yeah.

309
00:25:33,573 --> 00:25:36,201
‪If you release an album,

310
00:25:36,284 --> 00:25:39,329
‪it'll establish the two of you as a brand,
‪like I suggested before.

311
00:25:39,955 --> 00:25:43,500
‪It'll give the 80th anniversary festival
‪a huge promotional boost as well.

312
00:25:44,125 --> 00:25:45,919
‪That's a great idea.

313
00:25:46,878 --> 00:25:48,505
‪What do you think, Jeong-yo?

314
00:25:49,547 --> 00:25:52,842
‪Well, as long as the pianist agrees…

315
00:25:58,890 --> 00:25:59,891
<i>‪No, Pi-o.</i>

316
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:03,186
‪Why would you do this?

317
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:05,063
‪You should be steering clear of him.

318
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:07,065
‪Why do you keep
‪involving yourself with him?

319
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,900
‪Why are you playing with fire?

320
00:26:08,984 --> 00:26:11,152
‪You're only worried about getting caught.

321
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:12,988
‪You feel no guilt toward Jeong-yo, do you?

322
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:17,951
‪The only way I can make it up to him
‪is to perform well.

323
00:26:19,577 --> 00:26:21,413
‪What if he's up to something?

324
00:26:21,997 --> 00:26:24,499
‪I'm terrified
‪he's getting in your way on purpose.

325
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:28,628
‪Even if that's true, it can't be helped.

326
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:32,674
‪If I can be the fuel for his fire,

327
00:26:33,550 --> 00:26:34,759
‪I'll do it.

328
00:26:42,475 --> 00:26:43,518
<i>‪Eighty years ago,</i>

329
00:26:43,601 --> 00:26:47,856
‪through the scars of war,
‪music kept us breathing.

330
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:49,107
‪PRESS CONFERENCE
‪LEGACY & LEAP

331
00:26:49,190 --> 00:26:52,319
‪From a quiet, humble beginning,
‪the Hankook Symphony now stands

332
00:26:52,402 --> 00:26:55,488
‪as a globally recognized name
‪in the world of music.

333
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:56,614
‪3. A MESSAGE FROM THE FUTURE

334
00:26:56,698 --> 00:27:00,035
‪This festival will celebrate that journey

335
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:03,663
‪while laying the groundwork
‪for the next generation…

336
00:27:03,747 --> 00:27:05,540
‪Working with Maestro Kang

337
00:27:06,249 --> 00:27:07,917
‪always excites me.

338
00:27:08,501 --> 00:27:13,715
‪The way he continues to explore music
‪and isn't afraid to break the mold

339
00:27:14,424 --> 00:27:16,384
‪keeps me on my toes.

340
00:27:16,968 --> 00:27:19,346
‪I chose Pianist Kang Pi-o

341
00:27:19,429 --> 00:27:23,141
‪because beneath his refined
‪and disciplined performance

342
00:27:23,224 --> 00:27:24,809
‪lies a burning passion.

343
00:27:25,518 --> 00:27:27,645
‪As we all know, the finest performance

344
00:27:28,271 --> 00:27:31,524
‪comes from a cool head
‪and a passionate heart.

345
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:33,443
‪I am fully committed

346
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:36,237
‪to delivering a premiere

347
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:38,156
‪worthy of the composer.

348
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:52,295
‪Jeong-yo.

349
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:55,215
‪I'm a little upset.

350
00:27:56,841 --> 00:27:58,468
‪I saw the piece you composed.

351
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:01,137
‪I'm pretty confident I can play it well.

352
00:28:01,930 --> 00:28:05,475
‪But you didn't even consider me
‪and went straight to your friend.

353
00:28:06,810 --> 00:28:08,103
‪I'm sorry.

354
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:09,604
‪But I felt that the right person

355
00:28:10,730 --> 00:28:11,940
‪would be Mr. Kang here.

356
00:28:12,565 --> 00:28:13,400
‪I see.

357
00:28:14,484 --> 00:28:15,735
‪Come on, Mr. Do.

358
00:28:16,861 --> 00:28:18,780
‪You can't really complain

359
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:21,324
‪when you've been
‪Mr. Kang's favorite for years.

360
00:28:22,075 --> 00:28:25,245
‪Just let Pi-o and Jeong-yo
‪love each other in peace.

361
00:28:25,328 --> 00:28:27,747
‪Oh, is that how it is?

362
00:28:29,999 --> 00:28:33,753
‪Goodness, artists are so possessive
‪when it comes to premieres.

363
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:36,005
‪Jeong-yo, you'll need to step it up

364
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:39,134
‪if you're going to write pieces
‪for the musicians standing in line.

365
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,804
‪Anyway, I'm so happy.

366
00:28:42,887 --> 00:28:47,267
‪To think my students would turn around
‪and become my competitors…

367
00:28:47,350 --> 00:28:49,686
‪Isn't this what all teachers hope for?

368
00:28:51,271 --> 00:28:52,272
‪Pi-o.

369
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,608
‪Make sure to dominate the stage again

370
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:58,278
‪and keep me on my toes, okay?

371
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:00,238
‪Yes, sir.

372
00:29:01,656 --> 00:29:02,490
‪Hyun-soo.

373
00:29:03,158 --> 00:29:05,368
‪-Come over here.
‪-Yes, sir.

374
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:11,791
‪Look at that.
‪Mr. Kang still adores Hyun-soo.

375
00:29:13,209 --> 00:29:14,753
‪Oh, right.

376
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:18,631
‪Can we touch base while you practice

377
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:22,135
‪and talk about how
‪the piece is coming together?

378
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:24,179
‪Since it's my first piece,

379
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:27,557
‪I'd like us to discuss it
‪as if we're creating it together.

380
00:29:28,141 --> 00:29:29,017
‪Of course.

381
00:29:29,809 --> 00:29:31,019
‪I'll do that.

382
00:29:39,277 --> 00:29:40,361
‪All of them?

383
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:42,113
‪Yeah. All of them.

384
00:29:43,656 --> 00:29:46,951
‪Can't you at least accept the invitations
‪to Salzburg and Lucerne?

385
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:49,120
‪I don't want to lose focus.

386
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:51,539
‪Cancel all of my performances.

387
00:29:52,582 --> 00:29:54,250
‪And don't accept any new invitations.

388
00:29:55,710 --> 00:29:56,544
‪Please.

389
00:29:58,046 --> 00:29:59,088
‪Hey, guys.

390
00:30:01,090 --> 00:30:04,427
‪Why don't we send everyone off
‪and grab a beer?

391
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:06,679
‪I'm sorry.

392
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:09,265
‪I have something to do, so I need to go.

393
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:12,310
‪Come on, we don't get together
‪like this very often.

394
00:30:12,393 --> 00:30:13,561
‪Just stay a bit longer.

395
00:30:14,771 --> 00:30:15,730
‪I'm sorry.

396
00:30:16,523 --> 00:30:18,149
‪All right then. Get home safe.

397
00:30:18,233 --> 00:30:19,192
‪Okay.

398
00:30:37,252 --> 00:30:39,754
‪Sorry, guys.

399
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:42,298
‪Something urgent came up.
‪Let's grab a beer next time.

400
00:30:43,299 --> 00:30:45,009
‪-Okay, Mr. Do. Good night.
‪-Sorry.

401
00:30:59,107 --> 00:30:59,983
‪Ji-hye.

402
00:31:00,483 --> 00:31:01,526
‪Kang Ji-hye.

403
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:06,364
‪Pull it together.

404
00:31:13,913 --> 00:31:14,956
‪Here.

405
00:31:19,419 --> 00:31:20,336
‪Hyun-soo.

406
00:31:22,755 --> 00:31:23,590
‪Hyun-soo.

407
00:31:25,341 --> 00:31:26,301
‪Hyun-soo.

408
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:29,220
‪Hyun-soo.

409
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:32,724
‪Everyone…

410
00:31:34,767 --> 00:31:36,394
‪makes mistakes

411
00:31:37,395 --> 00:31:39,731
‪as they go through life, right?

412
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:44,694
‪I know.

413
00:31:46,613 --> 00:31:48,781
‪I know I'm a horrible person.

414
00:31:48,865 --> 00:31:49,991
‪I really do.

415
00:31:52,118 --> 00:31:53,202
‪But I had no choice.

416
00:31:54,996 --> 00:31:55,872
‪I had no choice.

417
00:31:55,955 --> 00:31:58,291
‪That's enough. Let's get you home, Ji-hye.

418
00:31:58,374 --> 00:32:00,209
‪Come on, get up.

419
00:32:02,587 --> 00:32:04,172
‪My poor Pi-o…

420
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:08,593
‪My poor, pitiful Pi-o…

421
00:32:11,054 --> 00:32:13,222
‪Please save Pi-o.

422
00:32:14,641 --> 00:32:17,226
‪Please get Choi Jeong-yo away from Pi-o.

423
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:18,728
‪I'm so scared.

424
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:21,773
‪I'm scared to death.

425
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:09,028
‪I wanted to see you today

426
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:14,158
‪because after the orchestra's
‪80th anniversary performance,

427
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:17,912
‪I'm going to step down
‪as artistic director.

428
00:33:18,955 --> 00:33:19,789
‪What?

429
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:21,499
‪I would like my successor…

430
00:33:22,834 --> 00:33:25,420
‪to be Choi Jeong-yo.

431
00:33:27,755 --> 00:33:29,298
‪What do you think?

432
00:33:29,924 --> 00:33:31,467
‪What do you mean?

433
00:33:36,222 --> 00:33:38,641
‪I'm against it. It's too soon.

434
00:33:38,725 --> 00:33:41,102
‪No, I've done enough.

435
00:33:41,769 --> 00:33:44,647
‪For the orchestra to turn a new page,

436
00:33:46,190 --> 00:33:48,317
‪it needs fresh talent.

437
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:52,030
‪And I think Jeong-yo is the right person.

438
00:33:52,113 --> 00:33:52,989
‪No.

439
00:33:54,574 --> 00:33:57,035
‪You can't retire
‪when you're still this healthy.

440
00:33:58,077 --> 00:33:59,287
‪Besides,

441
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:02,707
‪I'm only here
‪because I like making music with you.

442
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:04,834
‪You can't do this to me.

443
00:34:08,671 --> 00:34:09,505
‪By any chance,

444
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:12,258
‪are you feeling unwell?

445
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:14,969
‪Are you hiding something from me?

446
00:34:17,513 --> 00:34:19,515
‪Please tell me.

447
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:21,809
‪It's not like that.

448
00:34:24,937 --> 00:34:27,356
‪I'm leaving because there's nothing sadder

449
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,150
‪than an old man overstaying his welcome.

450
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:31,027
‪Try to understand.

451
00:34:40,536 --> 00:34:43,706
‪MAHLER'S SYMPHONY NO. 5, 4TH MOVEMENT
‪CONDUCTOR: KANG SEUNG-WOON

452
00:35:07,355 --> 00:35:08,231
‪Continuing from yesterday…

453
00:35:09,857 --> 00:35:12,693
‪Fourth movement, the <i>‪Adagietto</i>‪.

454
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:15,488
‪All right. Let's begin.

455
00:35:49,897 --> 00:35:52,191
‪Don't just play. Put more feeling into it!

456
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:02,243
‪Play the emotion, not just the notes!

457
00:36:15,923 --> 00:36:17,300
‪Do you know

458
00:36:18,301 --> 00:36:21,679
‪what's missing from our performance?

459
00:36:23,556 --> 00:36:25,850
‪You played the notes well.

460
00:36:25,933 --> 00:36:27,143
‪But can you make music…

461
00:36:29,312 --> 00:36:33,065
‪simply by following the markings
‪on the page?

462
00:36:34,108 --> 00:36:35,651
‪You see,

463
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:40,698
‪the <i>‪Adagietto </i>‪is a love letter
‪Mahler sent to Alma.

464
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:44,869
‪He loved her so much

465
00:36:44,952 --> 00:36:47,246
‪that he wrote her a musical love letter.

466
00:36:50,249 --> 00:36:51,417
‪But our performance…

467
00:36:53,419 --> 00:36:55,171
‪has none of that love.

468
00:36:59,175 --> 00:37:01,385
‪Stop obsessing over the notes,

469
00:37:01,469 --> 00:37:04,639
‪understand the emotions,
‪and pour your soul into it.

470
00:37:06,515 --> 00:37:08,726
‪The reason I keep nagging…

471
00:37:11,729 --> 00:37:15,650
‪is because I want you all
‪to own the music.

472
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:18,945
‪Each and every one of us

473
00:37:19,695 --> 00:37:21,447
‪must own the music

474
00:37:22,031 --> 00:37:26,160
‪for our energy to resonate
‪and move the audience.

475
00:37:26,744 --> 00:37:30,331
‪Picture the person
‪you love the most in the world,

476
00:37:30,414 --> 00:37:34,794
‪and imagine you're expressing
‪your deep love to them.

477
00:37:35,753 --> 00:37:36,671
‪Now then.

478
00:37:38,631 --> 00:37:39,924
‪Again, from the top.

479
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:30,284
‪NFCAPF STEERING COMMITTEE
‪KANG JI-HYE

480
00:39:32,995 --> 00:39:34,163
‪What is it?

481
00:39:34,246 --> 00:39:35,081
‪Hi.

482
00:39:36,082 --> 00:39:37,333
‪Ji-hye.

483
00:39:37,416 --> 00:39:40,252
‪Did you know your father is retiring?

484
00:39:41,253 --> 00:39:42,380
‪Retire?

485
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:43,547
‪Your father

486
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:47,218
‪is passing the baton to Jeong-yo
‪after the 80th anniversary performance

487
00:39:47,301 --> 00:39:48,594
‪and then retiring.

488
00:39:48,677 --> 00:39:50,846
‪Where is this coming from?

489
00:39:52,014 --> 00:39:54,058
<i>‪Do you think he's unwell?</i>

490
00:39:54,558 --> 00:39:57,269
‪He's passing the baton to Choi Jeong-yo?

491
00:40:00,022 --> 00:40:01,023
‪Father.

492
00:40:02,191 --> 00:40:05,486
‪There's no retirement age for a conductor,
‪so why are you stepping down?

493
00:40:05,569 --> 00:40:07,279
‪Who told you that?

494
00:40:08,489 --> 00:40:10,366
‪It was supposed to be a secret.

495
00:40:10,449 --> 00:40:11,784
‪Why is Choi Jeong-yo your successor?

496
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:15,413
‪There are so many conductors
‪hoping to succeed you.

497
00:40:15,913 --> 00:40:18,332
‪Why would you pass it on
‪to someone so inexperienced?

498
00:40:18,416 --> 00:40:19,875
‪What's the matter with you?

499
00:40:21,335 --> 00:40:23,462
‪Why do you hate Choi Jeong-yo so much?

500
00:40:23,546 --> 00:40:25,589
‪Does he have something on you?

501
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:28,759
‪Be kind.

502
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:32,096
‪Or else you'll make more enemies,

503
00:40:32,179 --> 00:40:34,849
‪and your child will end up with bad karma.

504
00:40:34,932 --> 00:40:37,226
<i>‪Do you still not know how the world works?</i>

505
00:40:48,821 --> 00:40:49,947
‪Sorry to keep you waiting.

506
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:51,699
‪I'm sorry.

507
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:54,827
‪Mr. Kang, did you get some practice in?

508
00:40:55,995 --> 00:40:57,037
‪Let's hear you play.

509
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:09,568
‪So?

510
00:42:12,446 --> 00:42:13,489
‪You didn't like it?

511
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:20,371
‪Maybe my expectations were too high.

512
00:42:20,871 --> 00:42:23,040
‪Or maybe you needed more time
‪to study the score.

513
00:42:23,123 --> 00:42:26,377
‪Your interpretation
‪sounded too superficial.

514
00:42:26,961 --> 00:42:30,548
‪I can't even give you feedback
‪at this point.

515
00:42:31,257 --> 00:42:34,093
‪Why don't you study it some more
‪and try again next week?

516
00:42:34,843 --> 00:42:35,678
‪Thank you.

517
00:42:40,724 --> 00:42:43,394
‪What exactly didn't you like?

518
00:42:43,477 --> 00:42:46,689
‪I did my best to interpret it
‪and practiced just as hard.

519
00:42:48,190 --> 00:42:51,652
‪But if I'm going in the wrong direction,
‪you should tell me why.

520
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:53,654
‪Oh…

521
00:42:55,072 --> 00:42:57,074
‪So this is what you call trying hard?

522
00:42:58,242 --> 00:43:01,161
‪Shall we go over everything
‪from the start then?

523
00:43:03,372 --> 00:43:05,666
‪Mr. Kang, what is the theme of this piece?

524
00:43:08,752 --> 00:43:11,338
‪The consequences
‪brought upon the arrogant.

525
00:43:13,215 --> 00:43:15,009
‪That's a convincing interpretation.

526
00:43:15,718 --> 00:43:19,888
‪Then why did you play
‪every phrase so beautifully?

527
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:22,850
‪With all your experience,

528
00:43:22,933 --> 00:43:26,729
‪why are you still hiding
‪behind that armor?

529
00:43:29,648 --> 00:43:30,482
‪I'll see you next week.

530
00:43:33,235 --> 00:43:34,320
‪Good work today.

531
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:35,446
‪Sorry about this.

532
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:44,580
‪So are you going to
‪take the structure completely apart?

533
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:47,958
‪-Yes.
‪-That's a great idea.

534
00:43:49,251 --> 00:43:51,253
‪A strong foundation
‪leads to better performance.

535
00:43:57,885 --> 00:43:58,719
‪Come in.

536
00:44:00,929 --> 00:44:01,847
‪It's a harpsichord.

537
00:44:18,906 --> 00:44:20,783
‪Can I practice on it for a few days?

538
00:44:20,866 --> 00:44:22,201
‪Of course.

539
00:44:22,284 --> 00:44:23,702
‪Thank you.

540
00:44:25,788 --> 00:44:26,830
‪Pi-o.

541
00:44:30,250 --> 00:44:31,251
‪Never mind.

542
00:44:31,335 --> 00:44:33,087
‪Just let me know when you leave.

543
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:36,507
‪I will.

544
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:59,738
‪Mr. Kang, what is the theme of this piece?

545
00:45:00,239 --> 00:45:02,908
‪The consequences
‪brought upon the arrogant.

546
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:07,162
‪Then why did you play
‪every phrase so beautifully?

547
00:45:13,335 --> 00:45:15,754
<i>‪With all your experience,</i>

548
00:45:15,838 --> 00:45:19,633
<i>‪why are you still hiding</i>
<i>‪behind that armor?</i>

549
00:46:19,401 --> 00:46:20,402
‪What do you think?

550
00:46:21,987 --> 00:46:23,906
‪Does it still sound superficial?

551
00:46:24,781 --> 00:46:25,616
‪No.

552
00:46:26,283 --> 00:46:27,284
‪I love it.

553
00:46:27,367 --> 00:46:30,746
‪It's more than that. It's really moving.

554
00:46:31,872 --> 00:46:33,957
‪This is why I like you.

555
00:46:34,041 --> 00:46:36,251
‪I really think you're a genius.

556
00:46:37,628 --> 00:46:39,546
‪No need to flatter me so much.

557
00:46:39,630 --> 00:46:40,964
‪Come on, I'm serious.

558
00:46:42,174 --> 00:46:45,135
‪I read the score before hearing you play,
‪and there's no disconnect.

559
00:46:45,219 --> 00:46:46,136
‪Really?

560
00:47:34,142 --> 00:47:35,269
‪What do you think?

561
00:47:36,645 --> 00:47:38,438
‪Let's hear the cadenza again.

562
00:47:55,163 --> 00:47:56,081
‪Too slow.

563
00:48:00,043 --> 00:48:01,211
‪Too fast.

564
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:04,548
‪It's slow.

565
00:48:09,636 --> 00:48:11,263
‪No, it's too fast!

566
00:48:13,599 --> 00:48:15,309
‪What do you think you're doing?

567
00:48:15,392 --> 00:48:17,019
‪How unprepared are you

568
00:48:17,102 --> 00:48:19,104
‪if you can't even
‪stay with the beat in the score?

569
00:48:19,187 --> 00:48:21,565
‪This is not the tempo I wanted.

570
00:48:23,483 --> 00:48:24,610
‪Try again and come back.

571
00:48:36,038 --> 00:48:36,913
‪Hey, Choi Jeong-yo.

572
00:48:40,709 --> 00:48:42,294
‪Explain it so that it makes sense.

573
00:48:44,546 --> 00:48:46,381
‪Here. This is 160.

574
00:48:46,965 --> 00:48:48,634
‪This is the tempo you wrote down.

575
00:48:48,717 --> 00:48:51,053
‪I practiced note by note to it.

576
00:48:51,136 --> 00:48:52,179
‪But you say I got it wrong?

577
00:48:52,679 --> 00:48:54,598
‪Which part did I play wrong?

578
00:48:54,681 --> 00:48:56,975
‪What is the tempo inside your head?

579
00:48:57,059 --> 00:48:57,893
‪Unbelievable.

580
00:48:59,811 --> 00:49:03,398
‪Why haven't you changed at all, Mr. Kang?

581
00:49:04,149 --> 00:49:05,317
‪Music is

582
00:49:06,902 --> 00:49:11,615
‪not a ready-made meal
‪you just heat up in the microwave.

583
00:49:11,698 --> 00:49:12,824
‪I'm begging you.

584
00:49:12,908 --> 00:49:15,035
‪Please feel the rhythm with your soul.

585
00:49:16,703 --> 00:49:20,332
‪How do you expect to fight and win
‪against a hundred orchestra members?

586
00:49:21,500 --> 00:49:22,542
‪Jeez.

587
00:49:32,552 --> 00:49:33,804
‪I don't get it.

588
00:49:35,055 --> 00:49:38,350
‪It sounded amazing to me.

589
00:49:39,351 --> 00:49:41,395
‪What was Jeong-yo not happy about?

590
00:49:42,646 --> 00:49:45,232
‪Do you want me to talk to him?

591
00:49:46,274 --> 00:49:47,192
‪No.

592
00:49:48,151 --> 00:49:50,737
‪I must've missed the composer's intent.

593
00:49:50,821 --> 00:49:52,322
‪I'll give it some more thought.

594
00:50:06,044 --> 00:50:07,087
‪Hey, what is it?

595
00:50:07,170 --> 00:50:08,422
‪There's a problem.

596
00:50:08,922 --> 00:50:11,758
‪Your dad disappeared,
‪and they haven't found him yet.

597
00:50:11,842 --> 00:50:12,718
‪What?

598
00:50:13,927 --> 00:50:15,095
‪When did he leave?

599
00:50:15,178 --> 00:50:16,263
‪I don't know.

600
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:18,932
‪He went for a walk after lunch
‪and vanished.

601
00:50:19,015 --> 00:50:20,142
‪They only just found out?

602
00:50:21,059 --> 00:50:22,477
‪Just wait. I'll be right there.

603
00:50:51,423 --> 00:50:53,049
‪Did they check all the local bars?

604
00:50:53,133 --> 00:50:55,802
‪Yeah, they searched everywhere,
‪but he's nowhere to be found.

605
00:50:56,762 --> 00:50:58,764
‪They're asking whether
‪they should report him missing.

606
00:50:58,847 --> 00:51:00,098
<i>‪Should we let them?</i>

607
00:51:00,182 --> 00:51:01,475
‪Just wait a bit.

608
00:51:02,559 --> 00:51:04,019
‪Let me go check out the situation.

609
00:51:32,798 --> 00:51:36,051
‪ALCOHOL REHAB CENTER

610
00:52:00,116 --> 00:52:01,618
‪What brings you here, Ms. Kang?

611
00:52:03,995 --> 00:52:05,914
‪Oh, Jeong-yo.

612
00:52:06,957 --> 00:52:08,458
‪Why are you here?

613
00:52:09,084 --> 00:52:13,296
‪The director here asked me
‪if I could perform for the patients.

614
00:52:14,005 --> 00:52:16,049
‪But why are you here, Ms. Kang?

615
00:52:16,132 --> 00:52:17,050
‪Oh, I…

616
00:52:18,093 --> 00:52:20,220
‪I know someone who's a patient here,

617
00:52:20,303 --> 00:52:21,721
‪so I came to visit them.

618
00:52:21,805 --> 00:52:23,640
‪At an alcohol rehab center?

619
00:52:25,225 --> 00:52:26,059
‪Yes.

620
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:29,980
‪It's amazing that you volunteer
‪despite your busy schedule.

621
00:52:32,023 --> 00:52:33,024
‪It's nothing.

622
00:52:34,025 --> 00:52:37,445
‪I'll need to hear the details
‪before I decide whether I can do it.

623
00:52:37,529 --> 00:52:38,488
‪Nothing's confirmed yet.

624
00:52:39,072 --> 00:52:40,073
‪I see.

625
00:52:40,156 --> 00:52:41,366
‪Still, it's amazing.

626
00:52:42,200 --> 00:52:44,744
‪I should get going. See you later.

627
00:52:45,328 --> 00:52:46,371
‪Goodbye.

628
00:52:58,300 --> 00:53:00,260
‪What's going on? Is she onto us?

629
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:04,806
‪Did you tell the staff to keep quiet?

630
00:53:04,890 --> 00:53:07,767
‪They won't say a word. Don't worry.

631
00:53:09,561 --> 00:53:12,147
‪But seriously, where did your dad go?

632
00:53:14,232 --> 00:53:15,442
‪MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

633
00:53:15,525 --> 00:53:17,485
‪Hey, I don't think he's here.

634
00:53:18,528 --> 00:53:20,739
‪Let's call the cops
‪and report him missing.

635
00:53:22,324 --> 00:53:23,783
‪Where the hell is he?

636
00:53:25,327 --> 00:53:26,202
‪Hold on.

637
00:53:27,829 --> 00:53:28,663
‪What is it?

638
00:53:30,040 --> 00:53:33,126
‪KIM'S BOILED PORK

639
00:53:35,253 --> 00:53:36,838
‪Is there a reason we're here?

640
00:53:38,423 --> 00:53:39,382
‪What the heck?

641
00:53:41,343 --> 00:53:42,677
‪How did you know he'd be here?

642
00:53:43,720 --> 00:53:45,305
‪Look at him, all carefree.

643
00:53:54,314 --> 00:53:56,691
‪-Mr. Choi, do you recognize me?
‪-Huh?

644
00:53:56,775 --> 00:53:58,735
‪-What do you want?
‪-Let's get you back to the hospital.

645
00:53:58,818 --> 00:54:01,237
‪No, I'm not going back to the hospital.

646
00:54:01,321 --> 00:54:02,906
‪You need to go. You're a patient!

647
00:54:02,989 --> 00:54:04,908
‪-No, I don't want to.
‪-Come on, let's go!

648
00:54:04,991 --> 00:54:06,576
‪I'm not going!

649
00:54:08,620 --> 00:54:11,748
‪-No, I don't want to go back.
‪-Hey, don't run off!

650
00:54:11,831 --> 00:54:14,334
‪-I said I'm not going back there.
‪-It's this way, man.

651
00:54:15,043 --> 00:54:17,587
‪Who's been paying my hospital bills?

652
00:54:18,421 --> 00:54:20,256
‪Stop messing around
‪and stay put, will you?

653
00:54:20,340 --> 00:54:22,217
‪-I said I'm not going back!
‪-In you go.

654
00:54:26,805 --> 00:54:27,764
‪Go home.

655
00:54:59,921 --> 00:55:01,047
<i>‪Music is</i>

656
00:55:02,632 --> 00:55:07,387
‪not a ready-made meal
‪you just heat up in the microwave.

657
00:55:07,470 --> 00:55:08,555
‪I'm begging you.

658
00:55:08,638 --> 00:55:10,682
‪Please feel the rhythm with your soul.

659
00:56:08,698 --> 00:56:09,657
‪What are you doing here?

660
00:56:10,867 --> 00:56:11,701
‪Pi-o.

661
00:56:14,788 --> 00:56:18,166
‪What if Choi Jeong-yo
‪doesn't have amnesia?

662
00:56:18,249 --> 00:56:19,417
‪Just stop already.

663
00:56:20,668 --> 00:56:22,629
‪Do you still want to
‪shift the blame to him?

664
00:56:36,309 --> 00:56:37,811
‪That's not it, Pi-o.

665
00:56:37,894 --> 00:56:39,687
‪Something's strange about him.

666
00:56:40,730 --> 00:56:42,440
‪He has amnesia but returned to Korea.

667
00:56:42,524 --> 00:56:45,068
‪Out of all the orchestras,
‪he chose the Hankook Symphony.

668
00:56:45,151 --> 00:56:46,236
‪But most of all,

669
00:56:46,945 --> 00:56:48,696
‪he keeps getting involved with you.

670
00:56:50,073 --> 00:56:51,574
‪Isn't that strange?

671
00:56:53,451 --> 00:56:55,370
‪I just couldn't figure him out,

672
00:56:55,453 --> 00:56:57,455
‪so I followed him last night.

673
00:56:57,539 --> 00:57:01,251
‪And I saw him go inside
‪an alcohol rehab center.

674
00:57:04,295 --> 00:57:05,588
‪You followed him?

675
00:57:08,216 --> 00:57:09,467
‪Just listen for a second.

676
00:57:10,426 --> 00:57:12,262
‪He somehow found out I was following him

677
00:57:12,345 --> 00:57:13,972
‪and suddenly showed up acting friendly.

678
00:57:15,223 --> 00:57:17,517
‪He doesn't know a single person in Korea,

679
00:57:17,600 --> 00:57:20,478
‪yet he went to the outskirts of Seoul
‪to do volunteer work.

680
00:57:20,562 --> 00:57:22,397
‪It makes no sense when he's so busy.

681
00:57:23,773 --> 00:57:25,275
‪It was weird how he blocked me.

682
00:57:26,025 --> 00:57:27,402
‪He's hiding something.

683
00:57:27,485 --> 00:57:31,030
‪He had a strange look in his eyes
‪when I saw him at the Seodam Art Center.

684
00:57:31,948 --> 00:57:34,534
<i>‪He left in the middle of the event,</i>
<i>‪went into a practice room,</i>

685
00:57:34,617 --> 00:57:36,494
<i>‪and stared out the window</i>
<i>‪through the curtains.</i>

686
00:57:36,578 --> 00:57:37,412
‪Jeong-yo.

687
00:57:38,288 --> 00:57:40,206
<i>‪He seemed very flustered when I walked in.</i>

688
00:57:40,290 --> 00:57:41,291
‪Could it be

689
00:57:42,250 --> 00:57:43,793
‪that his memory is back?

690
00:57:44,836 --> 00:57:47,172
‪His mom passed away
‪at the Seodam Art Center.

691
00:57:48,590 --> 00:57:50,383
‪There's no way he could forget that.

692
00:57:52,927 --> 00:57:53,845
‪Mom.

693
00:57:54,345 --> 00:57:56,055
‪Stop wasting your time imagining things.

694
00:57:56,639 --> 00:57:57,849
‪And stop following Jeong-yo.

695
00:57:59,184 --> 00:58:00,393
‪If you do that again…

696
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:04,147
‪I won't let it slide.

697
00:58:24,959 --> 00:58:28,213
‪Why haven't you changed at all, Mr. Kang?

698
00:58:36,804 --> 00:58:40,391
‪How do you expect to fight and win
‪against a hundred orchestra members?

699
00:58:40,475 --> 00:58:42,143
<i>‪So in a concerto,</i>

700
00:58:42,227 --> 00:58:45,563
‪a pianist has to fight and win
‪against a hundred orchestra members,

701
00:58:46,189 --> 00:58:47,774
<i>‪while still working together at times.</i>

702
00:58:48,399 --> 00:58:50,360
‪Avoiding a slump

703
00:58:50,443 --> 00:58:52,320
‪isn't going to solve anything.

704
00:58:52,403 --> 00:58:55,365
‪You need to face it at some point.

705
00:58:55,448 --> 00:58:57,909
‪Ignoring the problem won't solve anything.

706
00:58:58,910 --> 00:59:01,329
‪You need to face it at some point.

707
00:59:26,145 --> 00:59:27,772
<i>‪He's hiding something.</i>

708
00:59:27,855 --> 00:59:31,317
‪He had a strange look in his eyes
‪when I saw him at the Seodam Art Center.

709
00:59:40,702 --> 00:59:44,080
<i>‪What if Choi Jeong-yo</i>
<i>‪doesn't have amnesia?</i>

710
00:59:56,467 --> 00:59:58,469
‪Pi-o, let's make a promise.

711
00:59:59,053 --> 01:00:00,847
‪Let's play some more four hands

712
01:00:00,930 --> 01:00:02,974
‪even after the competition.

713
01:00:03,057 --> 01:00:03,891
‪Okay.

714
01:00:16,863 --> 01:00:19,741
<i>‪He left in the middle of the event,</i>
<i>‪went into a practice room,</i>

715
01:00:19,824 --> 01:00:21,576
<i>‪and stared out the window</i>
<i>‪through the curtains.</i>

716
01:00:27,373 --> 01:00:29,000
<i>‪He seemed very flustered when I walked in.</i>

717
01:00:29,083 --> 01:00:29,917
<i>‪Could it be</i>

718
01:00:31,210 --> 01:00:32,754
<i>‪that his memory is back?</i>

719
01:00:42,930 --> 01:00:45,350
<i>‪Promise you won't sulk</i>
<i>‪if I win first place.</i>

720
01:00:45,433 --> 01:00:46,851
<i>‪Let's still have fun when we hang out.</i>

721
01:00:46,934 --> 01:00:48,936
<i>‪But I'm going to win first place.</i>

722
01:00:49,020 --> 01:00:49,854
<i>‪Don't get sulky yourself.</i>

723
01:00:55,360 --> 01:00:58,154
‪SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK
‪FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

724
01:01:18,675 --> 01:01:20,802
‪FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

725
01:01:20,885 --> 01:01:22,595
<i>‪I know you remember everything.</i>

726
01:01:22,679 --> 01:01:24,639
‪Why did you tell such a lie?

727
01:01:25,431 --> 01:01:28,518
‪I don't understand what you're saying.

728
01:01:28,601 --> 01:01:31,688
‪We need to get rid of him
‪so he can't talk.

729
01:01:31,771 --> 01:01:32,980
‪Just call me Kim.

730
01:01:33,564 --> 01:01:36,859
<i>‪I didn't struggle to come back alive</i>
<i>‪just to give you a free pass.</i>

731
